\cf0      A fl\'91t resource definies the paramaters for a fleet, which is a collection of ships that can be made to appear randomly throughout the galaxy. Fleets can also be made to appear by including them in dude resources. \
\
LeadShipType	ID of the fleet's flagship's ship class\
\
\cf2 EscortType (x4)	IDs of the flagships escorts' ship classes. If you don't want to use four different escort types, you should still set the unused fields to a valid ship class ID. (you can set the min & max fields to 0 and just have the extra ships not appear)\cf0 \
\
Min (x4)		The minimum number of each type of escort to put in the fleet.\
\
\cf2 Max (x4)		The maximum number of each type of escort to put in the fleet.\cf0 \
\
G\'9avt			ID of the fleet's government, of -1 for none.\
\
LinkSyst			Which systems the fleet can be created in\
	\cf2 -1			Any system\cf0 \
	128-1127		ID of a specific system\
	\cf2 10000-10063	Any system belonging to this specific government\cf0 \
	15000-15063	Any system belonging to an ally of this g\'9avt\
	\cf2 20000-20063	Any system belonging to any but this g\'9avt\cf0 \
	25000-25063	Any system belonging to an enemy of this g\'9avt\
\
\cf2 MissionBit	-1		Ignored\cf0 \
		0-511		The fleet will only appear when this mission bit is set\
		\cf2 1000-1511	The fleet will only appear when this mission bit is not set\cf0 \
\
Note: The MissionBit field is ignored when the fleet is pointed to by a d\'9fde resource.\
\
Note: When setting up mission resources, you shouldn't make reference to a d\'9fde resource which contains pointers to fleets, as this will cause Override to behave strangely. Use only normal, single-ship d\'9fde resources in missions.}